From: RemoteOS maintainers <remoteos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dtls: require DTLS 1.2 for appliance media

OpenSSL's generic DTLS_method can allow DTLS 1.0. The appliance already
requires OpenSSL 3 and does not support legacy DTLS peers. Fail closed
when the minimum cannot be applied.

Upstream: Not submitted [product transport policy]

--- a/ext/dtls/gstdtlsagent.c
+++ b/ext/dtls/gstdtlsagent.c
@@ -190,6 +190,15 @@
 
     g_return_if_reached ();
   }
+  /* RemoteOS supports authenticated DTLS-SRTP with DTLS 1.2 or newer only. */
+  if (!SSL_CTX_set_min_proto_version (priv->ssl_context, DTLS1_2_VERSION)) {
+    GST_ERROR_OBJECT (self, "Unable to enforce DTLS 1.2 minimum");
+    ERR_print_errors_cb (ssl_warn_cb, self);
+    SSL_CTX_free (priv->ssl_context);
+    priv->ssl_context = NULL;
+    g_return_if_reached ();
+  }
+
   /* If any non-fatal issues happened, print them out and carry on */
   if (ERR_peek_error ()) {
     ERR_print_errors_cb (ssl_warn_cb, self);
